#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064033 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064150 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function"}] :question/id #uuid "e6c4219b-1955-5fa0-a362-6cc273510d88" :question/math-academy-id "e-258" :question/problem "The function $g(x)$ is given by\n![](images/c6/c67122865cc8decbb3238cd70c1fe662bdbcf9f697bd8a8e594e4408b88a08c3.svg)\nIf $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=2,$ what is the value $b?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $g(x)$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\sqrt{bx+3})=\\sqrt{2b+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x) & =g(2) \\\\ \\sqrt{2b+3} & =5 \\\\ 2b+3 & =25 \\\\ 2b & =22 \\\\ b & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064034 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50eadb82-ffa5-5ee5-b878-1c04e41fba7e" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b411bf9f-f944-505d-94dc-13df743545dd" :question/math-academy-id "e-259" :question/problem "The function $h(x)$ is given by\n![](images/d1/d113c9de6e0c7946ed9952a2a245f4ba0ebb627b74c4661a2a067216fe5099d8.svg)\n\nGiven that $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the value of $c?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $h(x),$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}{log}_{3}⁡(x+c) \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(0+c) \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}h(x) & =h(0) \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡(c) & =2 \\\\ c & ={3}^{2} \\\\ c & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $c=9$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064118 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c931e4a8-ad1d-5a5a-8f8f-f3901efda408" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Polynomial Function"}] :question/id #uuid "5443849c-193c-58a9-ae6c-1b859bbd1d4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6320" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n![](images/90/90209edc9ee3cc9c6c17b71427dc4dda0a14558a9df7b2a71dbe017073b9086a.svg)\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,1}({x}^{2}+2kx+1) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}+2k(1)+1 \\\\  & =2+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x) & =f(1) \\\\ 2+2k & =4 \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $k=1$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c931e4a8-ad1d-5a5a-8f8f-f3901efda408" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ae5a0c9-bf84-5a48-8994-bad74ebbc48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504168} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b0902-9401-50c5-a273-bde1a1c45b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504220} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf2b966-a18b-57ad-b7ac-fbcc3e618bb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504278} {:answer/id #uuid "cc42a784-e420-567f-9456-61d930539531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504379} {:answer/id #uuid "e8aaf60e-4bce-543c-895c-b179f6dd1cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b0902-9401-50c5-a273-bde1a1c45b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504220} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd804eaa-6ae9-5069-96e9-85f025f7e166" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b9e1a36-03a5-51c4-becb-f3f4b938141f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107604" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3a-2ax, & x\\ne -2, \\\\ 14, & x=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2,$ what is the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}(3a-2ax) \\\\  & =3a-2a(-2) \\\\  & =7a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-2,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x) & =f(-2) \\\\ 7a & =14 \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50eadb82-ffa5-5ee5-b878-1c04e41fba7e" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a368caa-071a-5e09-b895-f6fee3f0b562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504217} {:answer/id #uuid "9314c4b8-7707-5373-9534-1d40448d8d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504292} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b7b665-8ee1-53eb-8f95-7a0b77e77444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504326} {:answer/id #uuid "c58ce9c8-7667-5765-b9a9-b725886916c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504366} {:answer/id #uuid "efdf1a8b-3c3d-5e6c-971a-9dd68e5b7b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9314c4b8-7707-5373-9534-1d40448d8d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504292} :answer-field/id #uuid "726c20fa-e270-57b1-9453-2ca197a81f1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88e928a1-3941-5cdc-9fa6-49a8d4b468c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107915" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x-2}, & x\\ne 4, \\\\ c, & x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4,$ what is the value of $c?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x-2}={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=4,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}f(x) & =f(4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50eadb82-ffa5-5ee5-b878-1c04e41fba7e" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01384154-a073-56e0-9faf-43be4f562891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504032} {:answer/id #uuid "08ee82a2-784d-5e9b-adf7-eadff82d9072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504048} {:answer/id #uuid "24a0b4c2-0c8c-5103-9f4a-eed2189e8fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504095} {:answer/id #uuid "394f7ad5-b9aa-5163-b7f9-a244a184d786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504132} {:answer/id #uuid "b05ef87e-9cad-533d-bf6e-91d974d3d93f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01384154-a073-56e0-9faf-43be4f562891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504032} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0150772-06cd-545e-9657-56eec3250d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "215b8d43-0fa8-5bc5-9a2a-4cbd17fc3abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107916" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{cx+4}, & x\\ne -1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{27}, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1,$ what is the value of $c?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{cx+4}={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-1,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x) & =f(-1) \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-c} & =\\frac{1}{27} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4-c} & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3} \\\\ 4-c & =3 \\\\ c & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504617 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c931e4a8-ad1d-5a5a-8f8f-f3901efda408" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cabc6a1f-59e4-548f-b60b-756848c16e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cabc6a1f-59e4-548f-b60b-756848c16e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504377} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2892fc8-eeca-5693-ab46-741623b88ed6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "354ae055-47d1-5393-8d47-099f76806cac" :question/math-academy-id "q-342333" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6k-20{x}^{2}, & x\\ne 1, \\\\ -8, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to 1}(6k-20{x}^{2})=6k-20.\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x) & =f(1) \\\\ 6k-20 & =-8 \\\\ 6k & =12 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $k=2$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c931e4a8-ad1d-5a5a-8f8f-f3901efda408" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0839c675-f64b-541c-9740-93cd0d680619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0839c675-f64b-541c-9740-93cd0d680619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504047} :answer-field/id #uuid "4096d65b-7ea4-5ebe-ad37-2c678bbb3af7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504505} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6c09573-7ca5-5d62-9cb5-a86a8b682a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6c09573-7ca5-5d62-9cb5-a86a8b682a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504367} :answer-field/id #uuid "a60d2178-4da7-5a76-ae69-d2388f530073" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4cdcaf7-2982-5947-b7f9-f0933f5cb1a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-342456" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(a-x)^{2}-a, & x\\ne -3, \\\\ 9, & x=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3,$ **in ascending order**, what are the possible values of $a?$\n\n$a=$ \n{{field-1}}\nor\n$a=$ \n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -3}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -3}((a-x)^{2}-a) \\\\  & =(a+3)^{2}-a \\\\  & ={a}^{2}+5a+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-3,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -3}f(x) & =f(-3) \\\\ {a}^{2}+5a+9 & =9 \\\\ {a}^{2}+5a & =0 \\\\ a(a+5) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $a=-5$ or $a=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50eadb82-ffa5-5ee5-b878-1c04e41fba7e" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c39b1e86-fa2f-50b0-9ea5-c429866d8088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c39b1e86-fa2f-50b0-9ea5-c429866d8088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504365} :answer-field/id #uuid "155255f6-d53f-59af-ab74-6efb503e6d44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "571bd0c6-54b5-542b-a105-2bb5a6fcaaf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-342512" :question/problem "The function $g(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2x+a}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 36, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $g(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}{6}^{2x+a}={6}^{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x) & =g(0) \\\\ {6}^{a} & =36 \\\\ {6}^{a} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $a=2$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50eadb82-ffa5-5ee5-b878-1c04e41fba7e" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ef9605e-2699-5174-9d74-bcee640c79f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "127" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ef9605e-2699-5174-9d74-bcee640c79f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "127" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504173} :answer-field/id #uuid "e35ad816-07aa-5999-9c62-cec4f07d6b3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "060bce41-c046-5d08-898b-cfb8261e7661" :question/math-academy-id "q-342552" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡(2x+k), & x\\ne -1, \\\\ 3, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1,$ what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}{log}_{5}⁡(2x+k) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(k-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x) & =f(-1) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(k-2) & =3 \\\\ k-2 & ={5}^{3} \\\\ k-2 & =125 \\\\ k & =127.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $k=127$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064150 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98f4258c-1359-5f8c-a3d6-d5d1ca10743d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98f4258c-1359-5f8c-a3d6-d5d1ca10743d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504304} :answer-field/id #uuid "a888f715-749b-5e14-b3ed-043c4e528572" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0241cfe8-3868-5b51-b660-c610e52d9bb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342622" :question/problem "The function $h(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{x+a}-\\sqrt{2+a}}, & x\\ne 2, \\\\ 6, & x=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=2,$ what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the limit, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{x+a}-\\sqrt{2+a}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{x+a}-\\sqrt{2+a}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x+a}+\\sqrt{2+a}}{\\sqrt{x+a}+\\sqrt{2+a}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{x+a}+\\sqrt{2+a})}{(\\sqrt{x+a})^{2}-(\\sqrt{2+a})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{x+a}+\\sqrt{2+a})}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-2)}(\\sqrt{x+a}+\\sqrt{2+a})}{\\cancel{x-2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(\\sqrt{x+a}+\\sqrt{2+a}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2+a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}h(x) & =h(2) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2+a} & =6 \\\\ \\sqrt{2+a} & =3 \\\\ 2+a & =9 \\\\ a & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $a=7$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064150 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ede090-0e98-526f-95c9-95e8850bcb72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24ede090-0e98-526f-95c9-95e8850bcb72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504097} :answer-field/id #uuid "77bbd51e-5904-5d45-8bc3-de4505ff154f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1326dade-f2c7-5d3e-a020-cedd74fc345f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342648" :question/problem "The function $g(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x-b}-\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 10, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor what value of $b$ is the function continuous at $x=0?$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the limit, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x-b}-\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x-b}-\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}}{\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b})}{(\\sqrt{x-b})^{2}-(\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b})}{x-2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b})}{x(1-2x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{x}(\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b})}{\\cancel{x}(1-2x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x-b}+\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}}{1-2x} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{-b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x) & =g(0) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{-b} & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{-b} & =5 \\\\ -b & =25 \\\\ b & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $b=-25$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064150 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9e428ad-9c07-56ed-8bf4-e13088d624b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504375} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf30fe6-a21e-5d8a-9fed-9bd8b523ad15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504417} {:answer/id #uuid "ed779198-0b8f-5e47-8776-168f108d3b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504442} {:answer/id #uuid "f00fa024-d6a9-58c4-8dc2-66e4509286fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504449} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf121fa-bdd1-545c-88ca-8e4025b8f31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00fa024-d6a9-58c4-8dc2-66e4509286fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504449} :answer-field/id #uuid "640f8788-c88f-577c-8c39-875943c154fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "550986e3-6ff5-514b-90ba-699e6397aa6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48283" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+k}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 2, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+k})=\\sqrt{k}.\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x) & =f(0) \\\\ \\sqrt{k} & =2 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064150 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "059675b4-5317-52c5-9e12-a825b02e678a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504041} {:answer/id #uuid "331d3ba3-7d70-552c-9017-a789e832ecce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504119} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3dc435-4333-5003-b8cf-c80d000a682d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504309} {:answer/id #uuid "a1847f87-ec08-58e3-8324-c070554a3699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504321} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa20eb0-d1e6-5ca7-86c5-1fe41e49f4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "331d3ba3-7d70-552c-9017-a789e832ecce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504119} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2b2c06-359a-556f-b20c-5c316319fefe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c7cc171-f78e-5279-bfdd-075dc2385743" :question/math-academy-id "q-48417" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+k}-\\sqrt{k}}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 18, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+k}-\\sqrt{k}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+k}-\\sqrt{k}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x+k}+\\sqrt{k}}{\\sqrt{x+k}+\\sqrt{k}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+k}+\\sqrt{k})}{x+k-k} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{x}(\\sqrt{x+k}+\\sqrt{k})}{\\cancel{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+k}+\\sqrt{k}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+k}+\\sqrt{k} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x) & =f(0) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{k} & =18 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} & =9 \\\\ k & =81.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c931e4a8-ad1d-5a5a-8f8f-f3901efda408" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43052fb3-1854-5e7e-bb9d-dbeb22cbffac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504149} {:answer/id #uuid "7af4cbac-2231-59aa-b98c-1eaeccf62d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ or $-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504245} {:answer/id #uuid "89a95b89-c539-56ec-9a45-b66598490d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504271} {:answer/id #uuid "d36a115e-c06f-5d7d-ad82-ab15154423a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504393} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fbb3c0-9695-54c8-bde7-a83dcf8353e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ or $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89a95b89-c539-56ec-9a45-b66598490d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504271} :answer-field/id #uuid "236d6ea6-c4af-51d7-b742-a850f092344f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3bf93bdf-40a6-507b-8e4d-2fa269000a75" :question/math-academy-id "q-48495" :question/problem "The function $h(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(x-c)^{2}+1, & x\\ne 2, \\\\ 2, & x=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$, what are the possible values of $c?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $h(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}((x-c)^{2}+1) \\\\  & =(2-c)^{2}+1 \\\\  & ={c}^{2}-4c+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}h(x) & =h(2) \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c+5 & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c+3 & =0 \\\\ (c-3)(c-1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $c=3$ or $c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c931e4a8-ad1d-5a5a-8f8f-f3901efda408" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Polynomial Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa8e8c0-b857-5fc7-9ddb-8f30269b3912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ or $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504088} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec6e43a-1282-505f-9b6d-101bed32568c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504172} {:answer/id #uuid "94e1f41b-4668-5074-b579-ab1ca6705495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ or $-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504296} {:answer/id #uuid "d85420bf-7b69-56ba-80f4-239c87020d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504411} {:answer/id #uuid "effdc863-3ca9-54c2-93ff-84ad50e4f261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ or $-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94e1f41b-4668-5074-b579-ab1ca6705495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ or $-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504296} :answer-field/id #uuid "f02f4648-14e0-5805-a7dd-9867416c6557" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e241dd2f-cf9d-55b1-810e-b45db1f40880" :question/math-academy-id "q-48496" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(c-x)^{2}+3c, & x\\ne -1, \\\\ -5, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$, what are the possible values of $c?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}((c-x)^{2}+3c) \\\\  & =(c-(-1))^{2}+3c \\\\  & ={c}^{2}+2c+1+3c \\\\  & ={c}^{2}+5c+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-1,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x) & =f(-1) \\\\ {c}^{2}+5c+1 & =-5 \\\\ {c}^{2}+5c+6 & =0 \\\\ (c+2)(c+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $c=-2$ or $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50eadb82-ffa5-5ee5-b878-1c04e41fba7e" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28bfb878-d116-5da1-9fee-d2b65e89a110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504104} {:answer/id #uuid "370e9d6b-2f33-5aaf-afde-460829004686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504127} {:answer/id #uuid "7d20f992-30d4-5d65-b87e-1bacd33bdcc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504253} {:answer/id #uuid "a33f01a3-064b-547d-a6b4-4222a8515448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504323} {:answer/id #uuid "d75814c9-ace7-5611-86fa-6aa2f33bbe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a33f01a3-064b-547d-a6b4-4222a8515448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504323} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e20a55-64e5-5910-8426-c1682701f362" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "819d9389-7897-53fe-92be-f89ba9882964" :question/math-academy-id "q-48544" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡3(x-k), & x\\ne 1, \\\\ 2, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}{log}_{3}⁡3(x-k) \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡3(1-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x) & =f(1) \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡3(1-k) & =2 \\\\ 3(1-k) & ={3}^{2} \\\\ 1-k & =3 \\\\ k & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $k=-2$ removes the point discontinuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064150 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" :knowledge-point/title "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "386d38ac-8353-56d2-943b-bb09bc3eacb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504130} {:answer/id #uuid "643235b3-c922-5967-92b4-b1619dd84475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504205} {:answer/id #uuid "c15cf822-b2ea-5a6d-8c65-b1c57086c6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504362} {:answer/id #uuid "ee26a702-30a7-5d4a-9a5d-90dfa82d33ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504444} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8cedae-1eb2-5560-9e5d-b6e2abc7a092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "643235b3-c922-5967-92b4-b1619dd84475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504205} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a81ec9a-1083-525c-a359-960a0e91e26c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d67e759-1525-5679-9c05-4036359d7add" :question/math-academy-id "q-48574" :question/problem "The function $g(x)$ is given by \n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-\\sqrt{1-x}}{ax}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor what value of $a$ is the function continuous at $x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the limit, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-\\sqrt{1-x}}{ax} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-\\sqrt{1-x}}{ax}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{1-x}}{\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{1-x}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-(\\sqrt{1-x})^{2}}{ax(\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{1-x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{ax(\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{1-x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2\\cancel{x}}{a\\cancel{x}(\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{1-x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2}{a(\\sqrt{x+1}+\\sqrt{1-x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{a(\\sqrt{0+1}+\\sqrt{1-0})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}g(x) & =g(0) \\\\ \\frac{1}{a} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ a & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $a=4$ removes the point discontinuity."}]}
